  "description": "Shared contract for the channel editor field that edits the legacy `other` value while a typed config override (config.api_version, config.library_id, config.plugin) may also be stored. The relay prefers a non-empty override over `other` (middleware/distributor.go). Every frontend must display `displayed`, and saving with `edit` (null = an unrelated save that leaves the field untouched; a string = the new value typed into the field) must send `payload`. The backend must persist `payload` unchanged, and the relay must then use `effective`. `payload.override` null means the override key is absent from config. Consumed by Go and frontend tests; do not reformat case names.",
